      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r42-role-xv-1-initiates-of-the-scarab-sekhmet-terminator-cabals-r41-unit-xv-0-sekhmet-terminator-cabal-source" hidden="true">
          <description>Sekhmet Terminator | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 2 | 3 | 2 | 9 | 2+/4+
Sekhmet Inceptor | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 2 | 3 | 3 | 10 | 2+/4+
SCARAB OCCULT The Sekhmet Terminator Cabal is a Psychic Brotherhood. When the army is selected, assign the Cabal to one Prosperine Cult normally. The Cabal receives both the Cult Arcana and Cult Mastery benefits of its selected Prosperine Cult. The Cabal selects one psychic power from any of the normal ProHammer Psychic Disciplines available to Thousand Sons: • Biomancy • Divination • Pyromancy • Telekinesis • Telepathy Psychic Tests are taken using Leadership 9. While the Sekhmet Inceptor remains alive, the Cabal counts as Brotherhood of Psykers (Mastery Level 2), knows one additional psychic power from the disciplines above and takes Psychic Tests using Leadership 10. If the Inceptor is slain, the Cabal immediately returns to Mastery Level 1 and loses the second psychic power. PROSPERINE FORCE WEAPONS The Cabal uses the normal Prosperine Force Weapon rules from the Thousand Sons Armoury. A Psychic Brotherhood may attempt only one Force Weapon activation during each Assault phase. Activating the Cabal's Force Weapons counts as using one psychic power.
Force Organisation:
• Elites
• 0–1
Unit Composition:
• 5 Sekhmet Terminators
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• The Sekhmet Inceptor is a Character
Wargear:
• Cataphractii Terminator Armour
• Prosperine Force Weapon
• Foeblaster Boltgun
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Thousand Sons)
• Fearless
• Brotherhood of Psykers (Mastery Level 1\)
• Scarab Occult
OPTIONS
• The Cabal may include up to five additional Sekhmet Terminators for +60 points per model.
• Any model may replace its Prosperine Force Weapon with:
• Power fist ........................................ Free
• Chainfist ................................... +10 points
• Any model may replace its Foeblaster Boltgun with a Combi-weapon at the normal Space Marine Armoury cost.
• For every five models in the Cabal, up to two Sekhmet may replace their Foeblaster Boltgun with:
• Heavy Flamer ............................... +10 points
• Plasma Blaster ............................. +15 points
• Reaper Autocannon ......................... +20 points
• One Sekhmet Terminator may be upgraded to:
• Sekhmet Inceptor ........................... +20 points
• The Sekhmet Inceptor may take:
• Grenade Harness ............................ +10 points
• The entire Cabal may take:
• Teleportation Transponders ................. +15 points
DEDICATED TRANSPORT
The Cabal may select a Land Raider, Dreadclaw Drop Pod or Spartan Assault Tank where Transport Capacity permits.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="r42-role-xv-1-initiates-of-the-scarab-sekhmet-terminator-cabals-rite-note" name="Rite of War Interaction" hidden="false">
          <description>When the most powerful formations of the XV Legion were committed to battle, the Sekhmet and the Legion's greatest sorcerers could be concentrated into a single overwhelming psychic spearhead.
EFFECTS
ASTRAL WARFARE
The first two psychic powers successfully invoked by Thousand Sons Psykers during each player turn are ignored when determining the penalties caused by Disturbance in the Warp.
All other ProHammer psychic rules apply normally.
WREATHED IN LIGHTNING, THEY REND THE VEIL
All Thousand Sons units composed entirely of models wearing Terminator Armour gain Teleportation Transponders at no additional points cost.
Thousand Sons Independent Characters may purchase Teleportation Transponders for +10 points regardless of the armour they wear.
Whenever a unit or Character using these Transponders arrives by Deep Strike, it gains the Fear special rule and may re-roll Invulnerable Save rolls of 1 until the beginning of the next Thousand Sons player turn.
INITIATES OF THE SCARAB
Sekhmet Terminator Cabals may be selected as Troops choices and must fulfil the Detachment's compulsory Troops selections.
THE BIDDING OF THE CRIMSON KING
Magnus the Red may fulfil a compulsory HQ selection when using this Rite and does not occupy a Lord of War selection.
LIMITATIONS
The army's Warlord must be Magnus the Red, Ahzek Ahriman or a Thousand Sons Praetor.
A Thousand Sons Praetor selected as the Warlord may be upgraded from Mastery Level 2 to Mastery Level 3 for +25 points.
The Detachment may not contain more Vehicle units than units with the Legiones Astartes (Thousand Sons) special rule.
The Detachment may not include an Allied Detachment or Fortification.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="r42-role-xv-1-initiates-of-the-scarab-sekhmet-terminator-cabals-clone-cleanup" name="Builder compatibility" hidden="false">
          <description>Removed 1 obsolete armoury link(s) inherited from the generic source entry while creating this Rite-specific battlefield-role copy.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
